  "verbalization": "Cyclostachnine is shown to have multiple targets, including Tyrosine-protein kinase SYK and Solute carrier family 12 member 5, which in turn target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings suggest that Cyclostachnine may interact with components of the polycomb group (PcG) complex, which is involved in epigenetic regulation. The evidence is supported by multiple pathways, with the highest scores indicating a strong relationship between Cyclostachnine and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The mechanisms appear to involve targeting of the PcG complex through different molecular pathways, possibly through the modulation of protein activity or structure. The consistency across different targets and their subsequent interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex suggests a potential role for Cyclostachnine in modulating PcG function, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm these interactions.",
